00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.390
{Ah, ah! }Onee-chan!

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:42.870
The landlord always seems troubled when we’re around.{If we keep staying here, the owner will be troubled.}

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.020
We should leave.{let’s go now}

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:44.640
Okay.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.830
We need to hurry up and
find a new place to live, Asu.{I think we should find a place quickly.}

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.550
Kyo-chan! Asu-chan!

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.170
Hello!

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:04.700
You’re hauling around all that luggage!

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:06.710
You must be looking for somewhere to live, right?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.510
Well, yes.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.600
Well then, don’t look any further.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:15.130
It just so happens that the second floor of my house is open.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:20.040
Are you serious?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.650
Hey now, wait a minute.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:24.300
Yeah, hold on now.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.730
Kyou-chan and Asu-chan are going to live on <i>my</i> second floor.

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.050
No way!

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.670
My house is bigger and cleaner!

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.100
Well, uh… I won’t even charge you rent!

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:41.130
What? What’s this all about?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.030
Yeah! Just what are you thinking?

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:47.110
You listen here, Asu-chan and Kyou-chan will be living on my second floor, and moreover,

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:53.210
Somehow, it seems like everyone has heard that we have to move out of the apartment.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:58.880
Um, everyone, why do you
all know that we have to…

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:02.060
Um, eh… Well… About that…

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:05.360
The truth is, I was asked by Hayashi-san.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.630
Me too.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.280
By the landlord!?

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:09.390
Me too.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.100
Why does the landlord care about where the two of us—

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:15.930
Hayashi-san might not say anything,

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:20.100
but he worries about the two of you like you were his own grandchildren.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.570
It’s all because of what happened to Eriko-san and Mami-chan, I bet.{hah~ in this line, the honorifics actually balance out the line break}

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.860
Those names…

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:28.680
<i>Eriko!</i>

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:29.820
<i>Mami!</i>

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:35.330
They were Hayashi-san’s wife and granddaughter.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.580
We always thought the landlord lived alone!

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:41.100
It was a long time ago.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.540
There was an accident.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.460
It’s been 40 years since then.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:56.970
It was a terrible tragedy.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:03.250
The driver was in a huge truck.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.310
Hayashi was never a man of many words,

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:09.350
but nobody has seen him so much as laugh or even smile since that day.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:15.910
The three of them would always happily watch the sakura petals.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.840
Watching the sakura petals…{gah. I set myself up for this. Is it too late to opt for "cherry blossoms"?}

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:25.790
That sakura tree must hold many of the landlord’s precious memories.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:30.290
That’s why he would stare at the sakura tree so intently.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.660
So that’s how it was.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:36.300
If we don’t do something to stop that mansion from being built…

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.430
Onee-chan, let’s go!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:40.750
Asu!

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.920
Oba-san, can you please watch our luggage for us?{Obasan, can you put these luggage at your house for now?}

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.200
We’ll come back for it soon!

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.960
Hey, w-wait, you two!

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:52.070
Everyone, we’re sorry, but thank you for your trouble.

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:55.020
Asu, let’s go back to the apartment!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:06.040
All this time, I thought that you and I were all alone, Asu.{I’ve always thought… that as long as I’m together with Asu, I can survive anything.}

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:11.430
So I thought that as long as we were together, it wouldn’t matter where we were living.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.130
Onee-chan!

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:16.390
But when the landlord kicked us out,{But, Owner-san told us to move out first.}

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.430
while we were looking for a new place to stay, I realized something.{When I looked at the real estate houses I figured out something.}

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:25.570
I really love that apartment! When I think about it being torn down, I love it even more!{herp derp}

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:26.810
Yeah!

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.440
I want to live there forever!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.360
Me too, Onee-chan!

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.910
They’ve already started the demolition?

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:48.420
<i>Are we too late?</i>

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:54.920
Mr. Landlord!

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.840
Wh-Why are you two here?{Wh-what the, you two…!}

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.840
Please don’t let them tear down the apartment!{TEAR IT DOWN WITH YOUR BEAR HANDS HAYASHI-SAN}{does he hibernate in the winter?}

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:04.640
The sakura tree! Don’t cut down the sakura tree!

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.600
No way!{OH NOES}

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.190
Mr. Landlord! Why?!

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:17.850
I don’t plan on having the apartment torn down, you know.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.880
Huh? But just now—

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:23.320
Onee-chan, it looks like the building being torn down is the one next door.

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.340
You’re right.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:32.180
As you can see, mine isn’t the one that was sold.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:34.130
So the apartment is going to stay like it is?

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:38.270
Well then, why did you tell us to move out?!

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:43.120
Since next door has become a construction zone,{Living next to a construction zone…}

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.310
there’s bound to be a lot of traffic.

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.300
It’s too dangerous.

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:50.520
It was a terrible tragedy.

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:53.950
The driver was in a huge truck.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:58.120
You’ve already found a new place to live, right?

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.700
Don’t come back here again.

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.570
<i>That’s right.</i>

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:06.910
<i>The landlord is always looking out for us.</i>

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:13.220
<i>Two years ago, he was the only one who would rent us a room, even though we had no parents.{Two years ago, the only person that would take us in was Owner-san.}</i>

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:14.760
Asu.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:15.800
Onee-chan.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:20.930
We won’t move!

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:26.560
We love this apartment, the sakura tree, and you, Mr. Landlord.

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:30.640
B-But still…{OH GOD THE BLUSHING}

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.380
We’ll be very mindful of the traffic.{SUDDENLY BRITISH}

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:39.010
When spring comes, I really want to watch the sakura petals together with you, Mr. Landlord!{I want to see the sakura trees blossom with Owner-san.}

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:41.150
Please!

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.320
Fine, suit yourself.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:45.940
Hooray!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:51.440
Ah! Onee-chan, look!

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:56.690
Do you see the two flowers that blossomed before springtime?

00:19:56.690 --> 00:20:00.760
The landlord wrapped a little enclosure around them to protect them from the wind.

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:02.940
He really did!

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.380
<i>We’re just like those flowers.</i>

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.980
<i>The landlord is protective of us.</i>

00:20:10.210 --> 00:20:11.300
<i>That’s right.</i>

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:15.510
<i>The landlord is definitely protecting us.</i>

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:25.100
Asu, it looks like we have a little extra money left over this month.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.130
Is there somewhere you’d like to go?

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:27.950
Yes.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:29.040
Where?

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:32.790
I want to go to our apartment and stay there with Onee-chan.{argh fuck argh fuck etc}{I want to stay with Onee-chan here.}

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:35.500
This apartment is the best.{speaking of which is their TEREBII bigger or is that just me}

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:38.960
That sounds good to me.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:46.450
<i>The spring that will bring the sakura tree into full bloom is still far away,</i>

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:49.150
<i>and before that comes a harsh winter.</i>

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:54.590
<i>Even though our parents are gone, there is still
someone out there who will protect us from the cold.</i>

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:58.380
<i>There is someone who can understand that coldness.</i>

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:03.540
<i>Watching the sakura tree from the window of this apartment,</i>

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:07.110
<i>the two of us are definitely not alone.</i>

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:10.540
<i>This is what I’ve realized.</i>

